From 5ba9193efbab6bceb67e89eaa435abc7acca141d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Berliner <32103696+Styx85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:25:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] ggml-cuda: hip: float dequant mat-vec for Q6_K on GCN
 (ncols_dst=1)

Extend the GCN float mat-vec path (no dp4a, y read as f32) to Q6_K, modelled on the Vulkan shader
mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp. block_q6_K is 210 bytes, so 32-bit words are loaded as two 16-bit halves. Q6_K uses
2 rows per 64-thread block: on gfx90c 4 rows is slower than the dp4a mmvq path, 2 rows is faster.

gfx90c, Qwen3 0.6B Q4_K_M tg128: 84.6 -> 86.6 t/s (Q6_K kernels -3.5%, and quantize_q8_1 is no longer
needed when all mat-vecs use the float path); Qwen3 1.7B unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
